NEW_SECTION
/* Overlay
   Scoped to .mOverlay: "> div" made every <div> child of the host absolute and full-size.
   left:0 so a padded host is covered from its edge; border-radius:inherit follows a rounded host. */
.xOverlay > .mOverlay{
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 0;
    top:0;
    left:0;
    border-radius: inherit;
}
.xOverlay > .mOverlay::before{
    border-radius: inherit;
    content: '';

REASON
Three overlay faults: the selector matched every <div> child of the host, so with
addOverlay("last") the host's own content divs became full-size absolute layers; with no
left, the overlay started after the host's padding; and it ignored a rounded host. The
two app callers (app/api.myinvitees.com index pages) use "first" and only the overlay's
own element, so scoping to .mOverlay changes nothing for them except the left edge.
